    location: "Udaipur, India",
    narrative: "Udaipur is a city built on the edge of water, its palaces reflected in lakes that have no bottom you can find. It is a place that understands permanence — and impermanence — in equal measure. Sakshi and Rajat married here, at the hour when the city glows, and the water holds the sky.",
    pause: "Some days become the axis around which an entire life quietly turns. You do not always know which day it is — until you look back.",
    reflection: "The veil caught the wind on the rooftop, just once, and for a moment it looked like the beginning of something much larger than a wedding. It was. Every photograph we made that day is evidence of exactly that.",
